<http://data.silknow.org/object/98b6ac5f-3b1f-37f9-9f50-5a1cf9b96a74>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric, woven silk and metal thread.\nDisplayed behind glass. \nWarp: pink silk\nWeft: white, black, orange, blue, green silk; silver-gilt metal strip S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nSelvedge: 2 cotton cords.\nSmall repeating pattern in bands linked by very fine black stems which form a series of offset vertical lozenges.  The ground appears to be gold metal thread. There are three bands:\n[1] an 8-petalled rosette in pink and blue, next to a small pink rosette with blue centre and 4 serrated white leaves which is enclosed within a lozenge, next to a more pointed version of the first rosette which appears to be set within a circle of white leaves.\n[2] a small pink and blue rosette with 4 leaves inside a lozenge; a large pink rosette with blue centre and with tiny leaves springing from it, seemingly set within a circle of white leaves; a small blue rosette with pink centre and 4 leaves inside a lozenge.\n[3] a large blue star-like flower with pink centre, seemingly inside circle of leaves; small pink and blue star flower and 4 leaves inside lozenge; large pink rosette with blue centre inside circle of leaves."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/189d4f62-3e7d-3de3-b391-1c747bf8abf3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b45502dc-31d1-3288-a29c-76fb1f7f56ba> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric, woven silk and metal thread.\nDisplayed behind glass. \nWarp: pink silk\nWeft: white, black, orange, blue, green silk; silver-gilt metal strip S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nSelvedge: 2 cotton cords.\nSmall repeating pattern in bands linked by very fine black stems which form a series of offset vertical lozenges.  The ground appears to be gold metal thread. There are three bands:\n[1] an 8-petalled rosette in pink and blue, next to a small pink rosette with blue centre and 4 serrated white leaves which is enclosed within a lozenge, next to a more pointed version of the first rosette which appears to be set within a circle of white leaves.\n[2] a small pink and blue rosette with 4 leaves inside a lozenge; a large pink rosette with blue centre and with tiny leaves springing from it, seemingly set within a circle of white leaves; a small blue rosette with pink centre and 4 leaves inside a lozenge.\n[3] a large blue star-like flower with pink centre, seemingly inside circle of leaves; small pink and blue star flower and 4 leaves inside lozenge; large pink rosette with blue centre inside circle of leaves."@en ;
